resources.string:
## Examples of complete answers

### Example 1: simple query

```json
{
  "pre_text": "I am retrieving the list of your zones.",
  "data_commands": [
    { "type": "ZONES", "params": {} }
  ]
}
```

### Example 2: action with validation

```json
{
  "pre_text": "I am going to create a Finances zone with the euro icon. This zone will hold your budget tracking tools.",
  "validation_request": true,
  "action_commands": [
    {
      "type": "CREATE_ZONE",
      "params": {
        "name": "Finances",
        "description": "Budget tracking and savings",
        "icon_name": "euro"
      }
    }
  ],
  "post_text": "The Finances zone is ready to hold your tracking tools."
}
```

### Example 3: communication module

```json
{
  "pre_text": "Several zones are named \'Sport\'. Which one do you want to delete?",
  "communication_module": {
    "type": "MultipleChoice",
    "data": {
      "question": "Choose the zone to delete",
      "options": ["Sport (created on 15/01)", "Sport (created on 20/02)", "Cancel"]
    }
  }
}
```

## Query examples

### Example 1: listing the zones

```json
{
  "type": "ZONES",
  "params": {}
}
```

Returns every zone with its configuration.

### Example 2: retrieving the configuration of a tool

```json
{
  "type": "TOOL_CONFIG",
  "params": {
    "id": "tracking_weight_123"
  }
}
```

Returns the complete JSON config, including the extra_fields defined:
```json
{
  "name": "Daily weight",
  "type": "numeric",
  "unit": "kg",
  "extra_fields": [
    {"name": "mood", "display_name": "Mood", "type": "TEXT", "config": {"length": "UNLIMITED"}}
  ]
}
```

### Example 3: data filtered by period, with explicit fields

```json
{
  "type": "TOOL_DATA",
  "params": {
    "id": "tracking_weight_123",
    "fields": ["id", "timestamp", "data.value", "extra.notes"],
    "period_start": "2024-01-01T00:00:00+01:00",
    "period_end": "2024-02-01T00:00:00+01:00",
    "limit": 50
  }
}
```

Returns up to 50 entries, including extra when the tool has extra fields:
```json
{
  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "entry_456",
      "timestamp": "2024-01-01T08:00:00+01:00",
      "data": {"value": 75.5},
      "extra": {"mood": "stressed"}
    }
  ],
  "pagination": {
    "current_page": 1,
    "total_pages": 3,
    "total_entries": 127,
    "entries_per_page": 50
  }
}
```

### Example 4: retrieving a schema

**Config schema** (tool_instance_id optional):
```json
{
  "type": "SCHEMA",
  "params": {
    "id": "tracking_config_numeric"
  }
}
```

**Data schema** (tool_instance_id required for the extra fields):
```json
{
  "type": "SCHEMA",
  "params": {
    "id": "journal_data",
    "tool_instance_id": "tools_abc123"
  }
}
```

Returns the complete JSON schema with every field, constraint and custom_field (when tool_instance_id is given).

### Example 5: the tools of one zone

```json
{
  "type": "TOOL_INSTANCES",
  "params": {
    "zone_id": "zone_sante_123"
  }
}
```

Returns every tool configured in the Health zone.

### Example 6: retrieving IDs alone, for a deletion

```json
{
  "type": "TOOL_DATA",
  "params": {
    "id": "tracking_weight_123",
    "fields": ["id"],
    "period_start": "2024-01-01T00:00:00+01:00",
    "period_end": "2024-02-01T00:00:00+01:00"
  }
}
```

Returns every entry of the period. Then take the IDs alone and pass them to DELETE_DATA.

## Action examples

### Example 1: creating data in a batch

```json
{
  "type": "CREATE_DATA",
  "params": {
    "tool_instance_id": "tracking_weight_123",
    "tooltype": "tracking",
    "entries": [
      {
        "name": "Weighing",
        "timestamp": "2024-01-01T08:00:00+01:00",
        "data": { "value": 75.5 },
        "extra": { "mood": "calm" }
      },
      {
        "name": "Weighing",
        "timestamp": "2024-01-02T08:00:00+01:00",
        "data": { "value": 75.2 },
        "extra": { "mood": "stressed" }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

Creates 2 weight entries with extra fields. The schema_id is derived automatically from the config of the tool.

### Example 2: updating data (partial update)

```json
{
  "type": "UPDATE_DATA",
  "params": {
    "tool_instance_id": "tracking_weight_123",
    "tooltype": "tracking",
    "entries": [
      {
        "id": "entry_456",
        "data": { "value": 75.8 },
        "extra": { "mood": "calm" }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Partial update**: changes the value and the mood extra field alone. The other fields (name, timestamp, other data fields, other extra fields) keep their existing values.
Only the fields you supply are updated.

### Example 3: deleting data

```json
{
  "type": "DELETE_DATA",
  "params": {
    "tool_instance_id": "tracking_weight_123",
    "tooltype": "tracking",
    "ids": ["entry_456", "entry_789"]
  }
}
```

Deletes 2 specific entries.

### Example 4: creating a tool

```json
{
  "type": "CREATE_TOOL",
  "params": {
    "zone_id": "zone_sante_123",
    "tooltype": "tracking",
    "config": {
      "schema_id": "tracking_config_numeric",
      "data_schema_id": "tracking_data_numeric",
      "name": "Weight",
      "..."
    }
  }
}
```

Creates a tracking tool instance in the Health zone.

### Example 5: creating a zone

```json
{
  "type": "CREATE_ZONE",
  "params": {
    "name": "Finances",
    "description": "Budget tracking and savings",
    "icon_name": "euro"
  }
}
```

Creates a new themed zone.

## Time period examples

### Example 1: the whole of last week (relative period)

```json
{
  "type": "TOOL_DATA",
  "params": {
    "id": "tracking_weight_123",
    "fields": ["id", "timestamp", "data.value"],
    "period_start": "-1_WEEK",
    "period_end": "-1_WEEK"
  }
}
```

### Example 2: the last 7 days up to now (relative + NOW)

```json
{
  "type": "TOOL_DATA",
  "params": {
    "id": "tracking_weight_123",
    "fields": ["id", "timestamp", "data.value"],
    "period_start": "-7_DAY",
    "period_end": "NOW"
  }
}
```

### Example 3: since the start of the month (start alone)

```json
{
  "type": "TOOL_DATA",
  "params": {
    "id": "tracking_weight_123",
    "fields": ["id", "timestamp", "data.value"],
    "period_start": "0_MONTH"
  }
}
```

**Note**: `period_end` omitted = up to the last data available.

## Simple flow: query → answer

**User**: "What are my zones?"

**AI - turn 1**:

```json
{
  "pre_text": "I am going to retrieve the list of your zones.",
  "data_commands": [
    { "type": "ZONES", "params": {} }
  ]
}
```

**System**: returns a list of 3 zones (Health, Productivity, Leisure)

**AI - turn 2**:

```json
{
  "pre_text": "You have 3 zones configured: Health, Productivity and Leisure."
}
```

The flow stops, the user has their answer.

## Multi-step flow: explore → analyse → act

**User**: "Create a daily weight tracking in the Health zone"

**AI - turn 1**:

```json
{
  "pre_text": "I am first going to check that the Health zone exists and retrieve the schemas I need.",
  "data_commands": [
    { "type": "ZONES", "params": {} },
    { "type": "SCHEMA", "params": { "id": "tracking_config_numeric" } },
    { "type": "SCHEMA", "params": { "id": "tracking_data_numeric" } }
  ]
}
```

**System**: returns the zones and the schemas

**AI - turn 2**:

```json
{
  "pre_text": "Good, the Health zone exists. I am going to create the weight tracking with the right settings.",
  "action_commands": [
    {
      "type": "CREATE_TOOL",
      "params": {
        "zone_id": "zone_sante_id",
        "tooltype": "tracking",
        "config": {
          "schema_id": "tracking_config_numeric",
          "data_schema_id": "tracking_data_numeric",
          "name": "Daily weight",
          "..."
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "post_text": "Your daily weight tracking is active now. You can record your measurements in it."
}
```

**System**: success, the postText is shown

## Flow with error handling

**User**: "Delete the Work zone"

**AI - turn 1**:

```json
{
  "pre_text": "I am first going to check that the Work zone exists.",
  "data_commands": [
    { "type": "ZONES", "params": {} }
  ]
}
```

**System**: returns the zones, "Work" is not among them

**AI - turn 2**:

```json
{
  "pre_text": "The \'Work\' zone does not exist in your system. Your current zones are: Health, Productivity, Leisure. Do you want to delete one of those?",
  "communication_module": {
    "type": "MultipleChoice",
    "data": {
      "question": "Which zone do you want to delete?",
      "options": ["Health", "Productivity", "Leisure", "Cancel"]
    }
  }
}
```

**User**: picks "Productivity"

**AI - turn 3**:

```json
{
  "pre_text": "I am going to delete the Productivity zone. This will also delete every tool it holds.",
  "validation_request": true,
  "action_commands": [
    {
      "type": "DELETE_ZONE",
      "params": { "zone_id": "zone_productivite_id" }
    }
  ],
  "post_text": "The Productivity zone and its tools have been deleted."
}
```

**User**: confirms → the system runs it and shows the postText
